# Refactoring

- Remove all console logging
- Evaluate if functions can be simplified without losing functionality
- Evaluate if parts of the code is over engineered
- Evaluate that the correct components from /components are used
- Evaluate if the correct hooks from /hooks are used
- Make sure colors are referenced from the constants/Colors.ts file
- For animations use hooks/animations
- Evaluate if types from /types are used correctly
- Use memoize only when it provides measurable value
- Never reference color literals, use Colors.ts
- Evaluate if we are using functionality in /utils correctly
- Never change functionality when refactoring so that code breaks